# Upstream defaults, written literally. zellij's keys live in config.kdl, and a
# config that has never been edited does not contain them — so there is nothing
# to read back until you rebind something. The SCAN tab generates a probed file
# if you do.
name:    zellij
what:    a multiplexer that shows you its own keys. The tmux alternative
check:   zellij
install: see the help view — the download needs curl -4 on WSL2
docs:    the bar along the bottom of the screen, which is always current

= THE IDEA
Ctrl-p           | PANE mode — the bar changes to show what is now bound
Ctrl-t           | TAB mode
Ctrl-s           | SEARCH / scroll mode
Ctrl-o           | SESSION mode
Ctrl-h           | MOVE mode
Ctrl-n           | RESIZE mode
Esc              | back out of whatever mode you are in

= SESSIONS
Ctrl-o d         | detach; everything keeps running
Ctrl-o w         | the session manager

= PANES
Ctrl-p n         | new pane
Ctrl-p d         | new pane, split downwards
Ctrl-p r         | new pane, split to the right
Ctrl-p x         | close this pane
Ctrl-p f         | fullscreen this pane, again to restore
Ctrl-p arrow     | move focus in that direction
Ctrl-p w         | floating pane, on top of the rest
Alt-arrow        | move focus without entering a mode
Alt-n            | new pane, without entering a mode

= TABS
Ctrl-t n         | new tab
Ctrl-t x         | close tab
Ctrl-t r         | rename tab
Ctrl-t arrow     | previous / next tab
Ctrl-t 1         | jump to tab 1
Alt-t            | new tab, without entering a mode

= SCROLLING AND COPYING
Ctrl-s           | enter scroll mode
Ctrl-s PgUp      | page up through the scrollback
Ctrl-s e         | dump the scrollback into your editor
Ctrl-s Ctrl-c    | leave scroll mode
mouse scroll     | works without any mode

= RESIZING
Ctrl-n arrow     | grow or shrink in that direction
Alt-+ / Alt--    | resize without entering a mode
